From 89e181991b819be2c83fae5e3ab58eb7023716d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: noamblitz <noamblitz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 13:03:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Also strip undeclared fields from explicit $project +
 rename test class
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous commit closed the no-$project path but explicit $project
stages still leaked undeclared fields:
  {"$project": {"street": 1}}           # direct
  {"$project": {"renamed": "$street"}}  # rename bypass

Filter the $project spec before interpretation: drop any mapping whose
source field isn't in allowed_fields. Alias-prefixed sources
(e.g. $loc.name) and exclusions ({_id: 0}) pass through unchanged.

$match / $sort still execute against undeclared columns — that leaves
a "does this row exist" side-channel but no value leak in output.

Rename test class to UndeclaredFieldsNotReturnedTest to reflect the
security property being pinned, and add cases for the two explicit-
projection leak paths.
